<title>JAPAN: Japan May industrial output rises prelim 3.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan May industrial output rises prelim 3.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's industrial production in May rose a preliminary 3.8 percent from the previous month on a seasonally adjusted basis, the Ministry of International Trade and Industry (MITI) said on Friday.</p>
<p>MITI said in a statement that in general terms output is on a gradual rising trend.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of the preliminary monthly figures follows: Seasonally adjusted month-on-month changes (in pct), index base 1990:</p>
<p>				  MAY	 MONTH AGO     MAYINDEX</p>
<p> Output			 +3.8	-0.5	  104.5</p>
<p> Shipments		    +3.8	-2.8	  105.4</p>
<p> Inventories		  +1.9	+3.1	  108.5</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>  shipments ratio	   -2.2	+8.0	  112.2</p>
<p>Unadjusted year-on-year changes (in pct):</p>
<p>				  MAY	 MONTH AGO</p>
<p> Output			 +6.8	+4.8</p>
<p> Shipments		    +6.7	+4.4</p>
<p> Inventories		  -0.8	-2.2</p>
<p>Inventories to</p>
<p>  Shipments ratio	   -3.7	-1.9</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of MITI's forecasts for manufacturers' output:</p>
<p>Seasonally adjusted, month-on-month changes (in pct):</p>
<p>				  JUNE     JULY</p>
<p>				  -2.6     +0.9</p>
</text>
